{
  "group": "shipped JSON schemas",
  "description": "Hand-written conformance cases for the 12 shipped JSON schemas: the ones that carry JUDGEMENT \u2014 why a constraint matters, or where the shape/meaning split lies. Each schema gets an instance that must be ACCEPTED (which also serves as the seed for the generated tier) and instances that must be REJECTED, naming the constraint that did it.\n\nSCOPE, measured rather than claimed: these cases alone pin about 9% of the ~229 constraints the schemas declare. The mechanical remainder is generated into 11-schema-constraints.json, which lifts measured coverage to roughly 55%. Run `make mutation` for the current number and `python3 runner/mutation_sweep.py --holes` for the constraints still pinned by nothing \u2014 mostly branches under oneOf/anyOf, where a single-constraint reject case would be unsound because another branch still matches.\n\nValidated by runner/jsonschema_mini.py, a stdlib subset validator. It raises on any keyword it does not implement rather than silently passing, so a schema that grows one fails loudly.\n\nschemas/acs-messages.xsd is XML, not JSON Schema. It is NOT covered by this dataset \u2014 the plugin's validate_xml.py is an untested surface here.",
  "surface": "schemas/*.json",
  "covers": [
    "MAR-527",
    "MAR-530"
  ],
  "profile": "bare",
  "cases": [
